  "slug": "asia-shares-cautious-earnings-season-oil-slips",
  "headline": "Asian Shares Open Cautiously as Earnings Season Looms and Oil Slips",
  "socialHeadline": "Investors stayed on the sidelines Monday ahead of the US earnings season, with South Korea down 1.1% and crude sliding on confusion over an unconfirmed Trump energy-ceasefire claim and Gulf strikes",
  "summary": "Asian shares started Monday cautiously as investors braced for the US earnings season, which kicks off with the big banks on Tuesday. South Korea fell 1.1%, while oil slid \u2014 Brent down 1.1% to $103.50 and US crude 1.2% lower at $90.73 \u2014 amid confusion over an unconfirmed Trump energy-ceasefire announcement and strikes in the Gulf.",
  "body": [
   "Asian markets opened the week on a cautious note on Monday, October 12, with investors holding back ahead of the US third-quarter earnings season. America's biggest banks report on Tuesday, setting the tone for a reporting season Wall Street will read closely for signs of how the economy is weathering the autumn.",
   "South Korea was among the region's weakest performers, dropping 1.1% as the defensive mood spread across the region's trading floors.",
   "Energy markets added to the uncertainty. Brent crude slipped 1.1% to $103.50 a barrel and US crude fell 1.2% to $90.73, as traders weighed confusion over an unconfirmed energy-ceasefire announcement by US President Donald Trump against reports of continued strikes in the Gulf.",
   "With earnings, energy headlines, and geopolitics all pulling in different directions, Monday's session set up a week where Asian markets will take their cues from Wall Street's results as much as from their own fundamentals."
  ],
