 {
  "id": "art-0048-paris-market-fire-2026",
  "slug": "paris-oldest-covered-market-fire-enfants-rouges-2026",
  "headline": "Fire Destroys Paris's Oldest Covered Market, the March\u00e9 des Enfants-Rouges",
  "socialHeadline": "The historic March\u00e9 des Enfants-Rouges, founded in 1615, was completely destroyed by an overnight fire; no casualties reported",
  "summary": "A fire that broke out in the early hours of Monday, October 12, 2026, completely destroyed the March\u00e9 des Enfants-Rouges, Paris's oldest covered food market, officials said. No casualties were reported and the cause is not yet known.",
  "body": [
   "The fire was reported around 4:15am on Monday at the market on Rue de Bretagne in the 3rd arrondissement. The covered hall was completely destroyed and its metal structure partially collapsed inward, according to the Paris fire brigade.",
   "The market, founded in 1615 and listed as a historic monument since 1982, was one of the best-known food destinations in the Haut-Marais, home to stalls serving cuisines from around the world. Its name, meaning \"Market of the Red Children,\" refers to orphans in the area who once wore red clothing.",
   "Ariel Weil, mayor of Paris Centre, said the fire was under control but the market was \"totally destroyed,\" urging people to avoid the Rue de Bretagne area. Lieutenant Colonel Pierre de Bouvier of the fire brigade told reporters \"the market was completely destroyed,\" adding that \"nothing remains of the covered market.\"",
   "No one was injured apart from one firefighter who felt slightly unwell, and officials said the blaze did not spread to neighboring buildings. The cause of the fire has not been established."
  ],
