 {
  "id": "art-0049-alvarez-mbilli-riyadh-2026",
  "slug": "canelo-alvarez-mbilli-riyadh-october-31-fight-on-2026",
  "headline": "\u00c1lvarez vs M'billi Still On for October 31 in Riyadh Despite Airport Attacks, Promoter Says",
  "socialHeadline": "Turki Al-Sheikh says Canelo \u00c1lvarez will fight Christian M'billi in Riyadh on October 31 \"no matter what happens\" after Houthi strikes on the Saudi capital",
  "summary": "Promoter Turki Al-Sheikh said on Sunday that Sa\u00fal \"Canelo\" \u00c1lvarez still intends to face Christian M'billi in Riyadh on October 31, 2026, despite weekend attacks on the Saudi capital's international airport claimed by the Houthis.",
  "body": [
   "Al-Sheikh, chairman of Saudi Arabia's General Entertainment Authority, said in a social media post on Sunday, October 11, that \u00c1lvarez had told him he would \"still fight in Riyadh this October, no matter what happens,\" adding that the Mexican star \"fears nothing.\" \u00c1lvarez's camp did not comment.",
   "The bout, billed \"Mexico vs. The World,\" is scheduled for October 31 on DAZN pay-per-view, with the WBC super-middleweight title at stake. \u00c1lvarez (63-3-2, 39 KOs) is fighting for the first time since losing to Terence Crawford in September 2025; M'billi (29-0-1, 24 KOs) holds the full WBC title following Crawford's retirement in December 2025.",
   "The reassurance follows a Saturday strike on Riyadh's international airport that killed at least 12 people and wounded more than 300, according to Saudi authorities, with the Houthis claiming responsibility; a second attack on Sunday reportedly killed one more person and injured around a dozen. The figures are consistent with Saudi authorities' reporting of the attacks.",
   "If the fight proceeds as planned, it would be one of the highest-profile sporting events staged in the Saudi capital since the attacks began \u2014 and a test of the kingdom's ability to keep its entertainment calendar on track."
  ],
