 {
  "id": "art-0050-flyers-worst-start-2026",
  "slug": "flyers-0-5-2-worst-start-franchise-history-fire-tocchet-2026",
  "headline": "Winless Flyers Fall to 0-5-2, Worst Season Start in Franchise History",
  "socialHeadline": "Philadelphia's seventh straight loss to open 2026-27 drew \"Fire Tocchet!\" chants; coach: \"It's on me\"",
  "summary": "The Philadelphia Flyers lost 4-1 to the Carolina Hurricanes on Sunday, October 11, 2026, falling to 0-5-2 \u2014 the longest season-opening losing streak in franchise history \u2014 as home fans chanted for head coach Rick Tocchet's dismissal.",
  "body": [
   "The 4-1 defeat at Xfinity Mobile Arena was Philadelphia's seventh straight loss to start the 2026-27 NHL season (0-5-2), breaking the franchise record. The Flyers have been outscored 28-8 and are one of three winless teams in the league.",
   "The previous worst season starts in franchise history were six-game winless runs in 1999-00 and 2008-09 \u2014 and both of those teams recovered to make the playoffs, a precedent the current group will be hoping to follow.",
   "Frustration boiled over in the third period as sections of the home crowd chanted \"Fire Tocchet!\" and others booed the team off the ice. Tocchet took responsibility afterward: \"We owe the fans a better product on the ice\u2026 it's on me, I've got to take the blame.\"",
   "Captain Sean Couturier said the group was struggling for cohesion: \"We're out of sync right now\u2026 we're just not winning battles.\" Philadelphia has little time to regroup, with the schedule offering no soft landing."
  ],
