 {
  "id": "art-0051-wnba-finals-venue-2026",
  "slug": "atlanta-dream-wnba-finals-home-venue-uncertain-2026",
  "headline": "Atlanta Dream Still Searching for a Home Venue for the WNBA Finals",
  "socialHeadline": "With State Farm Arena booked for a concert and Hawks games, the Dream's home dates for the 2026 Finals were still undetermined Sunday night",
  "summary": "The Atlanta Dream had still not confirmed where they will play their home games of the 2026 WNBA Finals as of Sunday night, October 11, with their usual home, State Farm Arena, unavailable on the scheduled dates.",
  "body": [
   "The Dream face the Golden State Valkyries in the Finals. The Valkyries will host Games 1, 2, 5 and 7 at San Francisco's Chase Center, an 18,064-seat arena that sold out all season; Atlanta is due to host Games 3, 4 and potentially 6 on October 22, 24 and 29.",
   "State Farm Arena, the Dream's playoff home, is unavailable: a Sombr concert is booked for October 22, and the Atlanta Hawks play the Rockets and Cavaliers on October 24 and 29. The Dream announced last week that all their 2027 home games will be at State Farm Arena, but that does not help this month.",
   "The fallback is Gateway Center Arena in College Park, which seats 3,500 \u2014 where the Dream played 16 of their 22 home games this season \u2014 though the club is trying to move to a larger venue. Attempts involving Georgia Tech, Georgia State and Gas South Arena have not succeeded, and playoff games at State Farm Arena this year averaged 9,695 fans.",
   "The uncertainty is an awkward subplot for a Finals featuring stars Angel Reese and Rhyne Howard: whichever venue is chosen, thousands of fans who watched the playoff run downtown face a much smaller building."
  ],
