 {
  "id": "art-0056-philippines-social-media-bill-2026",
  "slug": "philippines-house-approves-under-13-social-media-ban-bill",
  "headline": "Philippine House Approves Bill Banning Social Media for Children Under 13",
  "socialHeadline": "The Philippine House of Representatives voted overwhelmingly to ban social-media access for children under 13",
  "summary": "The Philippine House of Representatives voted overwhelmingly on Monday to approve a bill banning social-media access for children under 13. The measure must still be reconciled with a stricter Senate version before going to President Marcos Jr.",
  "body": [
   "The Philippine House of Representatives voted overwhelmingly on Monday to approve a bill banning social-media access for children under 13, advancing one of Southeast Asia's most ambitious age-restriction measures for the internet.",
   "The Senate had previously endorsed a stricter version that would bar account creation for anyone under 18. The two chambers must now reconcile their versions in a bicameral conference before the measure goes to President Ferdinand Marcos Jr for his signature.",
   "## The trigger",
   "The debate reignited after three school shootings since June focused national attention on the effects of social media and online content on young people, according to reporting on the legislation.",
   "President Marcos Jr said on Sunday that he was studying the bill but cautioned that a blanket ban could drive children to hide their online activity \u2014 a signal that the final shape of the law is far from settled.",
   "## A global wave of age-gate laws",
   "The Philippines joins a growing list of countries weighing or enacting minimum-age rules for social media, as governments grapple with enforcement realities: verifying ages at scale, protecting minors' privacy in the process, and defining exactly which platforms count as social media.",
   "What remains: the bicameral reconciliation, the president's decision, and \u2014 if signed \u2014 the hard part of enforcement."
  ],
  "category": "World",
  "tags": [
   "Philippines",
   "Social Media",
