 {
  "id": "art-0057-nepal-budhi-gandaki-flood-2026",
  "slug": "nepal-flash-flood-budhi-gandaki-5-missing-rescues",
  "headline": "Nepal Flash Flood Sweeps Away Homes and Bridges; 5 Missing as Army Helicopters Race In",
  "socialHeadline": "A flash flood on Nepal's Budhi Gandaki river swept away homes and bridges, leaving 5 missing as army helicopters delivered aid to cut-off villages",
  "summary": "A flash flood along the Budhi Gandaki river in Nepal's Gorkha district on Sunday left five people missing, destroyed several bridges and dozens of houses, and damaged hydropower construction sites. The Nepal Army deployed helicopters to deliver food, tents and medicine to remote villages.",
  "body": [
   "A flash flood tore through villages along the Budhi Gandaki river in Nepal's Gorkha district on Sunday, leaving five people missing and sweeping away homes, bridges and infrastructure, the country's disaster management authority said.",
   "Nepal's National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Authority said the five missing people have not been found; no fatalities have been reported so far. Some 95 people were evacuated to nearby towns, including nine foreigners.",
   "## A landslide dam breach",
   "The flood was triggered when a landslide dam gave way near the village of Chumchure, sending a torrent down the Budhi Gandaki, the agency said. Several bridges were destroyed, dozens of houses swept away, and three hydropower-plant construction sites damaged, according to officials.",
   "Early-warning systems allowed most residents to reach higher ground before the water arrived \u2014 a factor officials credit with keeping the casualty count low.",
   "## Helicopters bring relief",
   "The Nepal Army deployed helicopters and ground troops to ferry food, tents and medicine to remote villages cut off by the flood, with operations continuing as rescue teams reached isolated communities in north-central Nepal.",
   "The missing-people and damage figures are preliminary and may change as assessments continue; NewsVeria will update this story with official figures."
  ],
