 {
  "id": "art-0060-ella-langley-tulsa-cancellation-2026",
  "slug": "ella-langley-cancels-tulsa-show-security-threat",
  "headline": "Ella Langley Cancels Tulsa Concert Over 'Serious Security Threat'; Police Find No Credible Danger",
  "socialHeadline": "Country star Ella Langley scrapped her Tulsa show two hours before showtime over a security threat \u2014 police swept the venue twice and found nothing credible",
  "summary": "Country music star Ella Langley canceled her October 9 concert at Tulsa's BOK Center about two hours before showtime, citing a \"serious security threat.\" Tulsa police said a threatening call warned of shots and bombs, but two sweeps with bomb-sniffing dogs found no credible threat \u2014 and police said they did not advise canceling the show.",
  "body": [
   "Country music star Ella Langley canceled her Friday concert at the Bank of Oklahoma Center in Tulsa, Oklahoma, about two hours before showtime, citing what her team called a \"serious security threat.\"",
   "Tulsa Police Captain Richard Meulenberg said the department received a threatening call warning of shots and bombs at the 19,000-seat venue. Officers conducted two sweeps of the arena with bomb-sniffing dogs and found no credible threat. \"Everything is safe,\" Meulenberg said \u2014 and police said they did not advise against holding the concert.",
   "## The artist's decision",
   "The cancellation was the artist's own precautionary call. \"I refuse to put anyone in harm's way,\" Langley, 27, said in her official statement. No rescheduled date had been announced as of the following day.",
   "The Tulsa Police Department and the FBI are investigating the threat call. Langley went on to perform her next scheduled show in Lubbock, Texas, on Saturday, where she addressed the cancellation on stage.",
   "The episode underscores how seriously venues and artists now treat threats made against live events, even when law enforcement finds nothing to substantiate them."
  ],
