 {
  "id": "art-0061-vance-firing-squad-remarks-2026",
  "slug": "jd-vance-firing-squad-execution-remarks",
  "headline": "JD Vance Casts Doubt on Pentagon's Plan to Livestream Fort Hood Shooter's Firing-Squad Execution",
  "socialHeadline": "Vice President JD Vance says he doubts the Pentagon will actually livestream Nidal Hasan's firing-squad execution \u2014 and he wouldn't watch it",
  "summary": "Vice President JD Vance told reporters on October 9 that he doubts the Pentagon's plan to livestream the firing-squad execution of Fort Hood shooter Nidal Hasan will actually happen, and said he would not watch it. The execution is scheduled for December 3, following Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth's announcement of a public broadcast that drew condemnation from the UN human rights office and others.",
  "body": [
   "Vice President JD Vance cast doubt on the Pentagon's plan to livestream the firing-squad execution of Fort Hood shooter Nidal Hasan, telling reporters in Cincinnati on October 9 that he was not convinced the broadcast would go ahead.",
   "\"I don't know that that's actually going to happen,\" Vance said of the proposed livestream, adding: \"I'm not going to be watching it.\"",
   "## A contested announcement",
   "Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth announced on October 8 that the execution, scheduled for December 3, would be shown publicly \u2014 the first US military execution since 1961 and the first military firing squad since World War II. The announcement drew swift condemnation, including from the United Nations human rights office.",
   "President Donald Trump later said he was \"yet to decide\" whether the execution would actually be shown publicly, appearing to walk back the Pentagon's position. Trump has publicly supported the firing-squad method.",
   "Hasan, an Army psychiatrist, was sentenced to death in 2013 for the 2009 Fort Hood attack in which 13 people were killed and 32 wounded, according to official records. (Trump has publicly put the death toll at 14; all official and reputable records state 13 killed and 32 wounded.)",
   "The debate over the broadcast has turned a military justice decision into a political flashpoint, with critics arguing that a public execution would serve no legitimate purpose and supporters framing it as accountability."
  ],
  "category": "Politics",
  "tags": [
   "JD Vance",
   "Nidal Hasan",
   "Death Penalty",
   "Pentagon"
  ],
  "author": "NewsVeria Newsroom",
  "publishedAt": "2026-10-12T14:05:00Z",
